Under 29 CFR 1910.132(d)(2), the employer must verify that the required workplace hazard assessment has been performed through a written certification [1]. 

This written certification must:
- Identify the workplace evaluated [1];
- Identify the person certifying that the evaluation has been performed [1];
- Identify the date(s) of the hazard assessment [1]; and
- Identify the document as a certification of hazard assessment [1].
